            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, a 38-year-old female, admitted on 16/09/2005 with acute lower abdominal pain and vaginal spotting. On admission, serum beta-hCG was markedly elevated. Transvaginal ultrasound confirmed a right-sided tubal ectopic pregnancy with no intrauterine gestational sac and free fluid in the pouch of Douglas, raising concern for early rupture. The patient was haemodynamically stable on admission. Given the clinical and sonographic findings, she was taken to theatre on 17/09/2005 and underwent laparoscopic right salpingectomy without intraoperative complications. Histopathology confirmed tubal ectopic pregnancy. Postoperative recovery was uneventful. She was discharged on 21/09/2005 in good condition. Please arrange follow-up including beta-hCG monitoring to confirm resolution and contraceptive counselling. I remain available for any queries.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
